safix::pass_entry_absent

  × the mapping 'grafana' is pass-to-safix, so the store is where its value
  │ comes
  │ from, and the store holds no entry at 'alice/grafana'. Nothing was
  │ written.
  │ 
  │ safix does not author that entry, and this is the one place the asymmetry
  │ shows: a value the operator puts in their own store is theirs to create,
  │ where a value safix mints is safix's. Create it, and the next run
  │ converges
  │ safix onto it.
  │ 
  │ If safix is the producer after all, the mapping is declared the wrong way
  │ round: mode = "safix-to-pass" makes the store follow safix.
